WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.080
- I have a question, when
creating "Mad About You,"

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.426
you pulled from your real life, so.

00:00:04.426 --> 00:00:05.259
- [Paul] It was the only thing I knew.

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:06.410
- What did your wife
think about that though?

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.243
'Cause you've been married for,

00:00:07.243 --> 00:00:08.850
is it 30-something years?

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.290
- Yes, 33 years.

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.730
My wife has no idea what
I do professionally.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.610
So the less, I keep her away...

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.035
When the show was on, I would
walk around the house, and no.

00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:19.530
(audience laughing)

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.363
No, she was great.

00:00:20.363 --> 00:00:21.900
She was actually instrumental

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.560
in finding Helen Hunt.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.823
We went to a,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.980
my wife and Helen had a mutual friend,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.150
and they had a dinner party.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.500
And this was just when I was
writing the first episode,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.770
and was thinking, you know,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.690
I really didn't know who it would,

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.800
I had no actress in mind,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.900
and met Helen, and she was
just funny and smart and just,

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.360
you know, just kooky enough

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.630
and off-balance enough and smart.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.037
And we left, and I said
to my wife, I said,

00:00:51.037 --> 00:00:52.500
"What do you think about her as you?"

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.850
She went, "She'd be great."

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.330
So she was, she was-

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.690
- So she gotta say.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.630
- Yeah, oh yes, I wouldn't,
I wouldn't, (laughs)

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.400
I wouldn't have cast somebody really,

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.600
if my wife said oh, I hate that person.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:03.970
But you know, the great thing was

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:05.750
we had so many great writers on the show,

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.680
and we'd all sit in the room,

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.540
and we'd all share our stories

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.660
of what happened at home that night.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.337
So if anything is too
personal, I could always go,

00:01:13.337 --> 00:01:15.900
"That was the other
guy's wife, that was...

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.567
You would never have said that."

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:18.490
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.410
- That's what songwriters do, by the way,

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.441
when you're in a
relationship with someone,

00:01:22.441 --> 00:01:23.274
and they're like, (laughs),

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:24.137
Why, people are gonna think I'm like,

00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:26.489
"Oh, that was the other
writer on the song.

00:01:26.489 --> 00:01:27.740
I would never say that."
- Always have backup

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.770
behind ya, yeah.
- Yeah, yeah. (laughs)

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:32.763
Throw someone else under the bus. (laughs)

